  </div>
</section>

<!-- Global Overview -->
<section id="global-overview">
  <h2>Global Homicide Rate Overview</h2>
  <p>From 1990 to 2023, the global <strong>median</strong> homicide rate among reporting countries fell from ''' + str(data['stats']['median_1990']) + ''' to ''' + str(data['stats']['median_2023']) + ''' per 100,000—a ''' + str(abs(data['stats']['median_change_pct'])) + '''% decrease. However, the global <strong>mean</strong> rate rose from ''' + str(data['stats']['mean_1990']) + ''' to ''' + str(data['stats']['mean_2023']) + ''', reflecting the outsized influence of a small number of extremely high-rate countries. The divergence between median and mean underscores that while the typical country became safer, severe violence concentrated in specific nations keeps the global average elevated.</p>
  <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartGlobalTrend"></canvas></div>
  <p>The peak global mean occurred in ''' + str(data['stats']['peak_year']) + ''' (''' + str(data['stats']['peak_mean']) + '''), driven partly by conflicts and institutional crises in several reporting states. Since the early 2000s, the median has trended steadily downward, suggesting broad-based improvements in public safety across the majority of reporting nations.</p>
  <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartCoverage"></canvas></div>
  <p>Coverage expanded from 47% of countries in 1990 to a high of 79% in 2010, but has since retreated to 42% in 2023. This decline in reporting capacity—especially after 2020—limits confidence in recent global aggregates and highlights the need for strengthened international data collection frameworks.</p>
</section>

<!-- Regional Comparison -->
<section id="regional-comparison">
  <h2>Regional & Country-Level Comparison</h2>
  <p>In 2023, the Caribbean recorded the highest regional median homicide rate (27.1), followed by North America (14.7) and South America (9.0). Europe and Asia reported the lowest median rates, at 0.9 and 0.9 respectively. These patterns are not merely geographic; they reflect differential capacities for law enforcement, socioeconomic development, and the presence of organized violence.</p>
  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartRegionalBar"></canvas></div>
    <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chartRegionalTrend"></canvas></div>
  </div>
